From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:50:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: s800x: Share the iPhone touchscreen and
 light sensor

The IPSW device trees of the six A9 iPhones (N66, N66m, N71, N71m, N69,
N69u) wire the touchscreen and the ambient light sensor the same way:
the controller on SPI2 with chip select AP GPIO 44, attention 142,
reset 75 and a 124 ns bit period, its analog supply from the Chestnut
display PMU and its core supply from the D2255's LDO 25; the light
sensor at 0x29 on I2C2 with its interrupt on AP GPIO 131. Move the
iPhone 6s Plus wiring into a file all of them include.

What differs is per model and comes from the same device trees and the
kernelcache's AppleMultitouchN1SPI personalities: the controller
(multi-touch,n66 C1F5C, n71 C1F5B, n69 C1F57, all with the same N1
clock values and addresses), its firmware and screen size, and the
light sensor (CT821 in the 6s and 6s Plus, CT819 in the SE). The
Samsung and TSMC builds of a model share one file.

Assisted-by: LLM
